<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/00031c6b06f4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Robodebt removed humans from Human Services, and the Government is facing the consequences" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/006dfacfdebc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Never mind that in their zeal, the Human Services Department would actually remove humans entirely from the process of identifying alleged debts and mailing what amounted to letters of demand to more than 370,000 people." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/015002539fbd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[924] ...this time by the external auditing firm PwC Australia, which has been engaged by the Department of Human Services." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "924" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/090531ef061f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Human Services Minister Alan Tudge has told his department to ensure welfare recipients can launch an internal review of their payments before debt proceedings are launched." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0bd26d9df0d0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink: Tax office says it cannot be blamed for automated debt recovery system's failings" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/115f9d5782d8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[924] ...this time by the external auditing firm PwC Australia, which has been engaged by the Department of Human Services." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "924" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1cc650e74462> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[915] Documents presented to Parliament by Human Services Minister Alan Tudge showed the use of automated data matching processes by Centrelink and the Department of Human Services resulted in 19,980 debt notices being issued..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/23b1ce63c475> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Australian Tax Office (ATO) has sought to distance itself from Centrelink's controversial debt recovery program, telling a Senate inquiry it cannot be held accountable for how its data is used." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/23bd11c75064> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[917] ATO officials claim there were no detailed conversations about how the Department of Human Services (DHS) would compare the ATO's annual income records..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/259ab73cc1bd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[915] Documents presented to Parliament by Human Services Minister Alan Tudge showed the use of automated data matching processes by Centrelink and the Department of Human Services resulted in 19,980 debt notices being issued..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29b55e9a05c7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[914] The Centrelink Online Compliance Intervention (robo-debt) program uses government records... to detect overpayments." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2bd2cfb38edb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Department of Human Services used the inquiry to highlight the changes it had made to the system, which it said had largely resolved the problems." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2ca1b795b119> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[924] ...this time by the external auditing firm PwC Australia, which has been engaged by the Department of Human Services." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "924" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e3195b804ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[924] Victoria Legal Aid has described Centrelink’s robo-debt system as an “abject failure”..." ;
