<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0113d8c053ec> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "‘Hit with a scary $25,000 demand’: Centrelink debt scandal hits Aboriginal communities" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "932" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/060c989e7f06> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ANDREW MEARES/FAIRFAX Kathryn Campbell Secretary Department of Human Services before a Senate Committee hearing into the Centrelink robo-debt collection in Canberra." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/09574f84cfca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Labor's shadow human services minister Linda Burney said the changes were a \"stunning admission\" given Mr Tudge's earlier claim the system was working." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0b2e764d82d2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Consumer Action Law Centre’s chief executive, Gerard Brodie, called on Centrelink to voluntarily ask the ACCC/Asic to hold it to the guidelines." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "924" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0b4c8fe386f2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Australian Greens Senator and Community Affairs References Committee chair Rachel Siewert, said the response showed contempt “for the thousands of Australians affected by this debacle”." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0ce639ad28f1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink debt recovery program to undergo changes following public criticism" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0d793ed19d51> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Independent MP Andrew Wilkie wrote to the Ombudsman on Monday, claiming Centrelink staff had told him that clients were feeling suicidal and let down by the system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1519b5cd260d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The system, which began last year, places a greater reliance on data matching to detect discrepancies between income reported to Centrelink and the Australian Taxation Office." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/155b8992286c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink robo-debt system wrongly targets Australian of the Year finalist" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "923" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1b0313ff0afb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink 'Robo-Debt' Program Unclear, Unreasonable And Unfair: Ombudsman" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1df8e3438a2d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Critics call it \"robodebt\", but how does the controversial system actually work?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "934" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e9ec16df091> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It removed a layer of human oversight from an automated data matching process, which compares an individual’s tax records with the earnings they have reported to Centrelink." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1f2ac24407a7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Nor had anyone evidently stopped to take rigorous legal advice on whether the brave new world of data-matched welfare recovery actually stood up to the laws of the land, which stand as the barrier between Government excess and the protection of the people." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/226364ce4455> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Deputy commissioner Greg Williams said he did not anticipate problems with the program because DHS had been using ATO data for more than 20 years." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/22c8d2b77ce5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We're all talking about the Centrelink debt controversy, but what is 'robodebt' anyway?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "934" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/232198902cac> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Department of Human Services, which looks after Centrelink, has a computer program that gathers data from other government agencies like the Australian Tax Office and then compares it with data that people have reported to Centrelink." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "934" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2484a83e8b19> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink loses more than one third of debt cases appealed to tribunal" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "925" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29797049a5d6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Robodebt removed humans from Human Services, and the Government is facing the consequences" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a7b0a7f7ba4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Independent MP Andrew Wilkie said he had been told by several Centrelink staff that the government is failing to properly deal with those left feeling suicidal by the system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "923" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/35a02b6cf805> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The official name is the Online Compliance Intervention." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "934" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/360252e0bf62> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Since July 2016, a total of 170,000 debt recovery notices have been sent out to Centrelink recipients informing them they had committed fraud for underreporting their income and demanding they pay back thousands of dollars or face debt collectors." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "932" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3f64ae5a3a44> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ATO officials claim there were no detailed conversations about how the Department of Human Services (DHS) would compare the ATO's annual income records of welfare recipients with its own periodic records." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4046889999ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink staff to strike over debt scandal, budget cuts and pay" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "931" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/42563023c2a9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Disability pensioner Justin Burns last week told the ABC he disputed his debt and requested a review, but was still being forced to pay $40 a fortnight from his pension to repay the debt while the review was underway." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/453b53b83955> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a media release, Labor MP Linda Burney said human services minister Alan Tudge needed to take action on the program’s failures." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/46ccbb862679> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[935] The automated program — which compares Centrelink and Australian Taxation Office records — has issued 170,000 notifications since July with thousands of Australians incorrectly told they have outstanding debts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/476cb8ddabb8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“The time taken to finalise a formal review depends on the complexity of the individual case. For the financial year to date, the average time to finalise a review in relation [to] debt decision was 49 days,” stated Department of Human Services General Manager, Hank Jongen." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "918" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4ee6b2e562ab> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Wilkie, who says he has spoken to several Centrelink whistleblowers, has written to the Commonwealth ombudsman detailing the allegations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "923" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/517ba933c091> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Senate inquiry calls for Centrelink robo-debt system to be suspended until fixed" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51cf2db1d26c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“The Turnbull government’s refusal to act on the recommendations of the Senate inquiry to overhaul the Online Compliance Intervention program is an insult to the thousands of decent Australians who were caught up in the conservatives’ robo-debt disaster.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51d1d5e4332e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink scandal: tens of thousands of welfare debts wiped or reduced" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51d54e44fdce> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Senate inquiry into Centrelink’s “robo-debt” system began on Wednesday, hearing from the community sector, the community and public sector union, tax office officials and the secretary of the Department of Human Services, Kathryn Campbell." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/53c1c84a907c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[912] The Community & Public Sector Union has demanded the federal government immediately suspend the automated big data system, which in the past week has been hammered for its lack of accuracy in determining debts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "912" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/55fc8cb091b6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Bill Shorten says 'Robodebt' scheme was illegal" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/576e5a4e43ad> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The [online compliance intervention] project effectively shifted complex fact-finding and data entry functions from the department to the individual and its success relied on its usability." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5a173d87dee7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A computer algorithm couldn't tell the difference between real and artificially calculated money \"owed\" in 470,000 cases." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5aa902984b94> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It's a newly automated debt recovery system that the Federal Government hopes will recover $4.5 million in welfare debt every day." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "934" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5ba753e835fe> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Commonwealth ombudsman has started investigating the Centrelink data-matching system, which has reportedly sent out more than 170,000 letters to customers accusing them of owing money or questioning their welfare eligibility." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "912" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/63612613ac00> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But Simon Rice, a professor of law at the Australian National University, explains that there's an exception for the welfare agency." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "934" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6637af35b7df> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Medical ethnographer Janet Hammill, 76, has spent decades researching the foetal origins of health and disease, and remains with the University of Queensland, where she works voluntarily and lives off the age pension." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "923" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/68e055c18d6a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink's debt recovery system lacks transparency and too difficult to use, ombudsman finds." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6b0e6b906a51> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The inquiry has urged all debts calculated using the error-prone “income averaging” process to be reassessed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6e803e40f9c1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NITV News has been inundated by stories from more than 100 people claiming they were erroneously told they owed Centrelink money." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "932" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/74da73a1aecf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A union claims almost every Centrelink debt letter is wrong and will bring a 'perfect storm' of complaints" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "912" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7563a6f2da53> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 client told the ABC they were contacted by debt collector Dun and Bradsheet about a $3,836 discrepancy, despite never being contacted by Centrelink." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7842b58ebb7d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink: Tax office says it cannot be blamed for automated debt recovery system's failings" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7bde426af200> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Led by its then-secretary Kathryn Campbell, the department was aiming for $300 million in the first six months of 2016-17, but had only landed $24 million in repayments." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/81156a9a1ce0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[921] A Senate inquiry has called for Centrelink’s controversial automated debt recovery system to be suspended until its many flaws can be resolved." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/82a212a1c0a5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When data differences are detected, the system generates a letter (this is not a debt letter) advising people of the difference and asking them to either confirm or update their details online using myGov." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "932" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/82edb2f17b83> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Greens senator Rachel Siewert was part of a Senate inquiry into Centrelink earlier this year." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "916" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/838c39699855> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Those are the findings of the Commonwealth Ombudsman's investigation into the Centrelink debt recovery scandal." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/87238d37d5ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Services Australia said in a statement that 470,000 debts would be waived, with refunds to be rolled out from July." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2168" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/882078505924> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This data matching process formed the basis of Centrelink's controversial debt recovery program, which was automated in mid-2016 in a bid to unlock savings." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/88fc0962e37f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Government Rejects Findings From Centrelink Robo-Debt Inquiry" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8929cba5800d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Government is using false figures to defend its robo-debt system" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "918" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8f46b5fa8aae> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The general idea of data matching to identify welfare overpayments, known as the Income Compliance Program, remains a cornerstone of government policy." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8f4b51121338> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Labor's Government Services spokesman Bill Shorten said the Government's backdown on the scheme should have come long ago." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2168" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9475af52ee87> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[921] The system removed a key layer of human oversight and placed greater reliance on a process of data matching, which automatically compared Centrelink and tax office records to detect discrepancies in reported income." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/982cbe704b2b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Government to pay back $721m as it scraps Robodebt for Centrelink welfare recipients" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2168" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/983918bab969> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The scheme saw hundreds of thousands of people issued with computer-generated debt notices, some of which made demands for payment from people who did not owe the Government any money." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2168" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9a69eac3f125> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Guardian Australia has reported on \"leaked advice prepared for ministers Robert, Anne Ruston and Christian Porter\" calling for Robodebts to be abandoned because the scheme was \"no longer viable\" or \"cost effective\" and would not rake in the money anticipated." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9f1ad9166330> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "DHS secretary Kathryn Campbell defended the program and dismissed calls for it to be immediately suspended." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9fc23ad7afc6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "If no response was received, Centrelink would use an “income averaging” method to calculate the debt." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a5b38328d79b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Administrative Appeals Tribunal has set aside 960 Centrelink debt decisions out of 2,699 appeals lodged between March 2016 and March 2017, while a further 132 were “varied”." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "925" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a7c910cfa70e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[914] The Centrelink Online Compliance Intervention (robo-debt) program uses government records... to detect overpayments." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a861ca1382a6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We’re asking customers to use the self-service options available through myGov and the Centrelink, Medicare and child support mobile apps, Jongen said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "931" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a9096581c174> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "'This is a joke': fighting Centrelink’s robo-debt, one year on" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "916" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/afc2accd3796> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Social Security Rights Network said the high rate at which the tribunal was setting aside or varying debt decisions was surprising." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "925" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b1a9f30a4dc4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Western Community Legal Centre’s chief executive, Denis Nelthorpe, said the level of legal assistance available to welfare recipients was extremely limited." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "924" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b8178bf1adc7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Labor’s Linda Burney has described the changes as a backflip, made after weeks of claiming there was nothing wrong with the system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "923" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b89a61a669a2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Government is using false figures to defend its robo-debt system" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "918" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bf8ec8c6abe0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Where a discrepancy in the two income records was detected, letters are automatically generated and sent demanding explanations from welfare recipients." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c1070a5192c0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The director of the ACT Council of Social Service, Susan Helyar, said cynics believed that may have been the government’s intent." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c314bd56e371> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Australian Council of Social Service's chief executive, Cassandra Goldie, said the figures further underlined the need for human involvement in debt decisions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "925" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c4172df743f3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a statement, Human Services spokesman Hank Jongen said an increase in referrals to social workers was related to family and domestic violence, rather than the debt recovery program." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c6d6af7575e7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Australian Council of Social Service chief executive, Cassandra Goldie, said on Wednesday said the system is unworkable and must be abolished." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cb0438b00983> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Welfare recipients to blame for Centrelink debt system failures, Senate inquiry told" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cbe10e3ca057> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Earlier, the Australian Council of Social Service (Acoss) said it feared the system’s treatment of welfare recipients was scaring individuals away from exercising their right to claim income support." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cc2b0bbc5c50> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sticking to the clawback system's proper name — the Online Compliance Intervention program — the inquiry found that despite Human Services pumping out \"please explain\" letters to people at an awesome rate of 20,000 a week, the robotic computers were already falling short of their human creators' expectations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ce5e2c896e55> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "20,000 people sent Centrelink 'robo-debt' notices found to owe less or nothing" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cf4e5660b5f0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[914] The Centrelink Online Compliance Intervention (robo-debt) program uses government records – matching and averaging a person’s income records held by Centrelink and the Tax Office – to detect overpayments." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d57149c8825b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Anglicare Australia released a similar statement on Wednesday, saying the system has unfairly shifted the onus of disproving debts onto vulnerable Australians." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dbb46b8ca567> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"The best advice we have is that raising a debt wholly or partly on the basis of ATO-averaged income is not sufficient under law,\" Government Services Minister Stuart Robert said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2168" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dc6810cbf65a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[919] Victoria Legal Aid’s executive director of civil justice, Dan Nicholson, said the most vulnerable and disadvantaged groups were less likely to have appealed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/decabb8e10b7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink robo-debt 'abject failure' and arguably unlawful, Victoria Legal Aid says" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "924" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ec160d4f838a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Launched in July 2016, the automated debt compliance system has been the subject of much scrutiny from its inception." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "918" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ec94e1f07cf9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ACOSS representative Susan Heylar said the program had undermined public confidence in the Government and left many welfare recipients worried about retribution." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fc9651c0c8ca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Greens Community Services spokeswoman Rachel Siewert said her party would work to ensure no person owed money was missed by the Government." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2168" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fd1ad939e972> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[917] ATO officials claim there were no detailed conversations about how the Department of Human Services (DHS) would compare the ATO's annual income records of welfare recipients with its own periodic records." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

