    airo:evidenceText "[935] The automated program — which compares Centrelink and Australian Taxation Office records — has issued 170,000 notifications since July with thousands of Australians incorrectly told they have outstanding debts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/15438cc662f5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[915] Documents presented to Parliament by Human Services Minister Alan Tudge showed the use of automated data matching processes by Centrelink and the Department of Human Services resulted in 19,980 debt notices being issued, all of which were either reduced or rescinded." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/31cb917bc4a8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ACOSS chief executive Cassandra Goldie said the Centrelink program had worried many Australians \"sick\", and accused the Government of cultivating a \"climate of fear\"." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/32b166462b16> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The department said the strike action had the potential to affect Centrelink, Medicare and child support services across the country." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "931" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/399f90ce371e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The system removed a key layer of human oversight and placed greater reliance on a process of data matching, which automatically compared Centrelink and tax office records to detect discrepancies in reported income." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3dfc63dab0e5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"The Government has an entitlement, a right, that ordinary people don't. It can convert an overpayment into a debt. The Social Security Act does that.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "934" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/437bf632f975> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hack has asked former Human Services Minister Alan Tudge, and the incoming minister, Michael Keenan, for comment on this story." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "916" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5836e0b6b3e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Community Affairs References Committee released a report in June into Centrelink’s controversial robo-debt program, making 21 recommendations to fix the program that was rolled out in mid-2016." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/676021681bec> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When the report was originally handed down in June, ACOSS CEO Dr Cassandra Goldie said the government needed to consider the report carefully and not extend the program." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7f3ff0638e05> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Commonwealth Ombudsman has launched an investigation into the Centrelink program and the National Audit Office is considering its own investigation." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9251a619176c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The story of how the data-matching scheme was invented with vim by a coterie of high-powered bureaucrats and sold to starry-eyed ministers is fabled in Canberra." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b803db3ecd5e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Federal Government will refund $721 million worth of debts it clawed back through its controversial Robodebt scheme." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2168" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c112d779f953> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serco Citizen Services – a subsidiary of multinational Serco – would be contracted to address issues with Centrelink’s call wait times, after it was recently revealed 42 million calls to Centrelink had gone unanswered over the last year." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c9359a91776d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[917] ACOSS chief executive Cassandra Goldie said the Centrelink program had worried many Australians \"sick\", and accused the Government of cultivating a \"climate of fear\"." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2db1214400b3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a joint statement, the shadow human services minister, Linda Burney, and the Labor MP Steven Georganas called on Tudge to apologise to the 20,000 individuals." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/73b45601523f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink has used data matching for a long time and as Human Services Minister Alan Tudge has pointed out, this particular algorithm was used by the previous Labor government." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "934" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9953218097c3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Those guidelines – produced by the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission and the Australian Securities and Investment Commission – prevent undue harassment, intimidation or unscrupulous practices, and requires private debt collectors to have evidence that a debt exists before they attempt to recover money." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "924" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f730f36813a6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Community and Public Sector Union (CPSU) secretary Nadine Flood said Centrelink was \"an agency in crisis\", with staff becoming expert in bandaid solutions to systemic policy failures." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "917" .

