    airo:evidenceText "Laura has engaged the services of Legal Aid and is appealing the debt." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "916" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/54fc38450373> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Labor has called for the system to be suspended while an investigation into its efficacy and accuracy continues, to which Mr Tudge replied: “… frankly, I don't think many taxpayers would support that call”." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "918" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/55b622ae5da8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It places a greater reliance on data matching to detect discrepancies between income reported to Centrelink and the Australian Taxation Office." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/73ef84fa85ef> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Human Services Minister Alan Tudge is still defending the system, despite his admission that the program has some flaws." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "918" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/76abb47e780a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The head of the Department of Human Services has blamed the “robo debt” scandal largely on welfare recipients’ failure to engage with Centrelink." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7fe58fb79992> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink should also consider paying back the ten per cent 'debt recovery fee' which was automatically applied to debts when the automated system was introduced -- and which the Human Services Minister Alan Tudge was reportedly himself unaware of when questioned by journalists in December." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/89b993006536> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Centrelink was relying on addresses it held on its own records, not the electoral roll, to target people who had stopped receiving benefits years ago." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/90ce458cb97c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As treasurer in 2016 and social services minister before then, Mr Morrison joined a long line of ministers, including Christian Porter, Alan Tudge and Stuart Robert, who believed in the promise of automated welfare debt recovery." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/968e957c2c50> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scott Morrison championed the program as social services minister and treasurer." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1160" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/98a68ed56f7b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When the Department of Human Services (DHS) was asked exactly how much debt has been reclaimed, it was unable to provide an estimate." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "918" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9ff9c4bb6c91> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hundreds of them made personal submissions last year to the Senate inquiry into public-sector bargaining, telling their personal stories of financial hardship and their worries about the enterprise agreement being pushed by their bosses." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "931" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a1b033b10df2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Turnbull government has admitted it issued robo-debt recovery notices to 20,000 welfare recipients who were later found to owe less or even nothing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/06af57188fd1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The scathing assessment came as the system is again put under the microscope, this time by the external auditing firm PwC Australia, which has been engaged by the Department of Human Services." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "924" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/874cbe3deed9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Department of Human Services staff will strike over pay, budget cuts and the Centrelink “robo debt” scandal, which together form an “ideological attack” by the Turnbull government, according to the Community and Public Sector union.",
        "Department of Human Services staff will strike over pay, budget cuts and the Centrelink “robo debt” scandal." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "931" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9f305c61bd14> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Community & Public Sector Union has demanded the federal government immediately suspend the automated big data system, which in the past week has been hammered for its lack of accuracy in determining debts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "912" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a17ad2d32db4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The government and the department of human services has defended the system — which combines Centrelink data with Australian Taxation Office records — citing that 80% letter recipients have paid the debts.",
        "The government and the department of human services has defended the system — which combines Centrelink data with Australian Taxation Office records — citing that 80% of letter recipients have paid the debts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "912" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/44076cccf35b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "However this response has been slammed by Labor and the Greens, who have labelled it as “grossly inadequate”." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4a23f7716271> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Victoria Legal Aid has described Centrelink’s robo-debt system as an “abject failure” which is an arguably unlawful response to the government’s self-inflicted budget problems." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "924" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/98294729618f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Centrelink Online Compliance Intervention (robo-debt) program uses government records – matching and averaging a person’s income records held by Centrelink and the Tax Office – to detect overpayments." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d91884537733> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Victoria Legal Aid’s executive director of civil justice, Dan Nicholson, said the most vulnerable and disadvantaged groups were less likely to have appealed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/43e335985d58> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The automated program — which compares Centrelink and Australian Taxation Office records — has issued 170,000 notifications since July with thousands of Australians incorrectly told they have outstanding debts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4a5a4b7f0498> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Senate inquiry has called for Centrelink’s controversial automated debt recovery system to be suspended until its many flaws can be resolved." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "921" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a511b97acf26> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The automated debt recovery system has drawn criticism from welfare organisations and is subject to an ongoing Senate inquiry." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "925" .

